// A tie out of a two-note tremolo's last note unfolds the tremolo (OMR, 2026-10-24).
// Bar 1: no tie, drawn as two dotted quarters joined by the tremolo beams (right).
// Bar 2: the same with b'16~ tied into the chord after it: Lily# 0.14.0 draws six beamed
// sixteenths (g'' b' g'' b' g'' b') and the tie. LilyPond 2.26.0 keeps the tremolo.
// From kinkel10-4 (MuseScore), bar 9's right hand: g''. b'.~ <b' g''>4 with a fermata.
octave absolute
time 6/8
part rh { clef treble }
section A {
  rh {
    repeat tremolo 3 { g'''16 b''16 } <b'' g'''>4 r8 |
    repeat tremolo 3 { g'''16 b''16~ } <b'' g'''>4 r8 |
  }
}
score { staff rh }